Read part of one entry without extracting it, as text, hex or base64. An offset is reached
by decoding up to it, since a compressed entry can't seek.

Usage: beezip read [OPTIONS] <ARCHIVE> [ENTRY]

Arguments:
  <ARCHIVE>
          The archive

  [ENTRY]
          The entry's path. With duplicates, the last copy; use `index` for another

Options:
      --index <INDEX>
          The entry's index in archive order, as `archive.list` shows it

      --offset <OFFSET>
          Where to start, in bytes

      --max-bytes <MAX_BYTES>
          At most this many bytes [default: 65536; at most 16 MiB]

      --encoding <ENCODING>
          How to return the data [default: text]

          Possible values:
          - text:   UTF-8, with invalid bytes replaced (and `lossy` set)
          - hex
          - base64

  -p, --password <PASSWORD>
          The password for an encrypted entry

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --output <FORMAT>
          How to print results; ndjson streams every job event

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   One JSON document on stdout: the output, or `{"error": {...}}`
          - ndjson: Every job event as a JSON line on stdout, ending with `Finished`, `Failed` or
            `Cancelled`
          
          [default: human]

  -q, --quiet
          No progress bars or info messages; warnings still print
